=====================================================================
C. CALCULATION SCREEN
=====================================================================

C1. Scenario selector
- Selected scenarios stay INSIDE the dropdown field as capsules
  (p-multiSelect display="chip"), followed by the "Add scenarios" placeholder.
- Each capsule has its own colour, assigned by selection order (background / text /
  border):
  1 blue   #EEF4FF / #1D4FB8 / #C9DAF8
  2 teal   #E8F7F4 / #0F766E / #B9E6DD
  3 purple #F3EEFF / #6D28D9 / #DCCEFB
  4 amber  #FFF4E5 / #9A4A00 / #F6D9AE   (then repeat)
- While a run is active: capsules show a lock instead of ✕, field read-only.

C2. Scenario persistence (option b)
- Save the selected scenario(s) AND the last readiness result with its timestamp in
  sessionStorage, per calculation type.
- When the user returns, restore both and DO NOT call readiness again.
  Hint under the selector: "↺ Restored from your last visit. Readiness result from
  <time>; it re-runs only on Check again, Reset or a new scenario."
  Readiness header shows "Last checked <time>".
- Re-run readiness only when the user changes the scenario, clicks Reset or clicks
  "Check again". (The backend still re-checks readiness when Run is clicked, so a
  stale cached result can never start an invalid run.)

C3. Reports card
- Download icon BEFORE each label: "⤓ Pre-Tax Segment", "⤓ Post-Tax Segment".
- On click: that button shows a spinner + "Generating…" and is disabled; under the
  buttons show a shimmer bar (light blue animated gradient):
  "Generating <report> report for <scenario>…".
- When the file is downloaded: green box "✓ <report> report downloaded." for 4 seconds,
  then hide. On error: red box with the error message.
- Post-Tax Segment is enabled after a successful run (see Backend).

C4. Readiness phase
- Do NOT show the execution stage list during readiness.
- While checking: only ONE spinner (in the hint "Checking readiness…"). Stepper shows
  "Readiness · Checking…". Criteria rows show grey name + grey skeleton line, nothing
  on the right (remove the right-side per-row spinners).
- When done: Met / Warning tags on the right of each criterion; header shows
  "<n> Met" and "<n> Warning" tags, "Checked <time>" and a "↻ Check again" button.

C5. Warning dialog "Run on unchanged data?"
- Header: amber circle "!" icon + title + ✕, bottom border.
- Body (13px): "Data for <scenario> hasn't changed since the last run. Running again
  replaces the previous results." Then a grey info box: "Last run  <date time> ·
  Run <runId>". Then the required checkbox "I understand this re-runs the calculation
  on unchanged data."
- Footer on a light grey background, right aligned: Cancel (outlined grey) and
  Run anyway (primary, disabled until the checkbox is ticked).

C6. Execution phase
- Show the 10 stages only after Run calculation is clicked / a run is triggered.
- Stage name 12.5px semibold (bold); message under it 12px normal weight, grey (same
  as readiness messages); duration on the right in monospace.
- Current stage: light blue row, blue name, spinner icon, live timer.
- Pending stages: grey name, "Pending".
- This styling must apply WHILE running, not only after completion.

C7. Calculation output (Result Aggregation) – same rows, modern table
- Keep the data exactly as today: one row per Entity / Tax Segment / Reporting Line,
  columns PQ1…PQn in the same order. No grouping or summaries.
- Section header: "Result Aggregation · <scenario>" + "<n> rows" tag; right side:
  search (entity, segment, line), "Run <runId>", Hide data, Segment summary report.
- Table header: two rows – a year band row (2026 / 2027 / 2028 …, small uppercase
  grey, spanning its quarter columns) and the column row ("PQ1" bold + "3Q2026" grey).
  Header stays visible on vertical scroll.
- Freeze Entity, Tax Segment and Reporting Line on horizontal scroll (p-table frozen
  columns) with a thin right border and soft shadow; visible horizontal scrollbar.
- Reporting Line shown as a small grey label (EBT / ETR / LLR / Taxes).
- Numbers right aligned, monospace, negatives in red (#B4233C), values as returned.
- Rows 34px, zebra striping, thin dividers, light blue hover, thin vertical divider
  between years.
- Paginator below: "Rows per page" dropdown with 100 / 150 / 200 / 250
  (default 150), "Showing x–y of n", page buttons. Keep the choice for the session.
- No full-screen view for now.

